        {
          "id": "the_link_is_on_network_which_is_what_this_slice_rests_on",
          "description": "A10, allocation.rs:631-682: an on-network link takes SourceHours = SHO and the off-network one takes SHP. The link's road type is 4, so the indicator is 1 and the two activity relations are the same numbers row for row -- which makes E1's ratio EXACTLY 1 and the F12-blocked soak fractions enter at a computed zero. What breaks if this is wrong: on an off-network link the denominator would be `population x noOfRealDays - SHO`, 6,902,112.67 h against 594.23 h at hourDayID 75, so `fractionOfOperating` would be 8.6e-05 and every soak weight would come alive -- and this document does not compute SHP, so it emits not-a-number there rather than reusing SHO. docs/evap-leaks.md 0.3.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
