        },
        {
          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_reference",
          "description": "A1 through A10 at the three ages docs/evap-leaks.md 6.0 tabulates, in both day types. The snapshot's own `sho` table -- which this document does not read -- stores 27.33, 2.43728, 260.057 and 23.1918 against the values pinned here; the differences are 6.7e-08 to 1.2e-06, which is that column's six-significant-figure storage (7.1). What breaks if this is wrong: every factor of A5 through A9 is in these four numbers. A6 as the harmonic mean instead of the arithmetic one is 24% and 58% low and A8 divides by it; omitting A7's weeksPerMonth divisor is 4.43x; normalising A3 over the run's source type instead of its HPMS group is 2.55x. The independent reproduction in 6.5 reaches the same four values to the last bit, from the same tables by a different route.",
