        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_movesoutput",
          "description": "L9 and O1 at the eight cells docs/evap-leaks.md 6.1 to 6.3 derive by hand, in both day types. The snapshot stores 1.70768, 8.43008, 4.92007, 0.00120038, 6.49975, 32.0866, 18.7267 and 0.00456889 against the values pinned here; the worst difference is 3.7e-06, which is the reference's six-significant-figure storage of its own intermediates and not accumulated error (7.1 attributes each residual to a specific stored column). What breaks if this is wrong: every factor of the whole chain is in these numbers. The independent reproduction in 6.5 reaches the same eight values to the last bit from the same tables by a different route, which is what makes a disagreement here attributable to the document rather than to the specification.",
