          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_im_blend_is_the_identity_because_the_program_table_is_empty",
          "description": "L1 and L9's trailing UPDATE. `imcoverage` has zero rows, so its discovered axis is zero-length, the aggregate over it reads the additive identity, and `im_blend` returns the unblended quantity -- which is the SQL's `a row with no matching cell keeps its value unchanged`, as a measured 0 rather than an assumption. What breaks if this is wrong: `pollutantprocessassoc` marks polProcessID 113 `isAffectedByEvapIM = 'Y'`, so this is an absent PROGRAM and not a structural exclusion, and a county with an evap I/M program would blend. The blend's argument order is unobservable at a zero fraction -- measured on the component, swapping the two rate arguments sends every non-probe row to exactly 0 rather than perturbing it -- so components/liquid_leaking_emissions.esm carries the probe row that pins the order, and this test pins only that the fraction really is zero and that the row count it comes from really is zero.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 18.726686295997105,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 41
              }
            }
          ]
        }
